15 0 obj
<<
/A 49 0 R
/Alt (Flowchart detailing a process that integrates datasets and deep learning models. The WEASD chest dataset undergoes preprocessing, then passes through a one-dimensional convolutional neural network. This leads to t-SNE and base CNN transfer with ScientISST-MOVE. Explainable AI with GradCam produces an output. The Dreamer dataset is preprocessed by removing irrelevant columns and signal extraction, followed by feature engineering. This includes statistical, wavelet, and Fourier transform-based features. The temporal conformer predicts VAD, followed by rule-based emotional interpretation, leading to emotional state diagnostics and unsupervised clustering for output.)
/K 0
/P 7 0 R
/Pg 35 0 R
/S /Figure
/T (Figure)
>>
endobj
16 0 obj
<<
/A 49 0 R
/Alt (Flowchart of a convolutional neural network architecture, displaying three blocks. The first block includes input layer, Conv1D, batch normalization, max pooling, and dropout. The second block repeats Conv1D, batch normalization, max pooling, and dropout. The third block has global average pooling, dense layer with ReLU, dropout, and a final dense layer with softmax activation.)
/K 0
/P 7 0 R
/Pg 36 0 R
/S /Figure
/T (Figure)
>>
endobj
17 0 obj
<<
/A 49 0 R
/Alt (t-SNE scatter plot visualizing CNN feature embeddings with clusters represented by different colors. Orange represents "run," pink for "walk_after," purple for "baseline," and light green for "walk_before_downstairs." A vertical color bar on the right corresponds to class labels.)
/K 0
/P 7 0 R
/Pg 37 0 R
/S /Figure
/T (Figure)
>>
endobj
18 0 obj
<<
/A 49 0 R
/Alt (Three line graphs are displayed. The first graph shows training and validation accuracy over 45 epochs, with accuracy improving and stabilizing above 90%. The second graph presents training and validation loss, both decreasing over epochs, with validation showing more fluctuations. The third graph depicts a declining learning rate across epochs from nearly 0.001 to below 0.00001, descending in steps.)
/K 0
/P 7 0 R
/Pg 41 0 R
/S /Figure
/T (Figure)
>>
endobj
19 0 obj
<<
/A 49 0 R
/Alt (Confusion matrix showing classification results for three classes. Class 0: 10,401 correct, 247 misclassified as Class 1, 98 as Class 2. Class 1: 3,438 correct, 21 as Class 0, 1 as Class 2. Class 2: 6,116 correct, 18 as Class 0, 8 as Class 1. Color gradient indicates frequency.)
/K 1
/P 7 0 R
/Pg 41 0 R
/S /Figure
/T (Figure)
>>
endobj
20 0 obj
<<
/A 49 0 R
/Alt (Confusion matrix showing predicted activities versus true labels for four actions: run, walk after, baseline, and walk before downstairs. The diagonal represents correct predictions, with run having the highest at 10,235. Other cells show varying numbers of misclassifications. A color gradient indicates frequency.)
/K 0
/P 7 0 R
/Pg 42 0 R
/S /Figure
/T (Figure)
>>
endobj
21 0 obj
<<
/A 49 0 R
/Alt (Graph showing two lines: a blue line representing the signal \(Channel 0\) fluctuates initially, spikes, then stabilizes towards the bottom. A red line for the Grad-CAM heatmap \(resized\) starts fluctuating, flattens, and stabilizes near the top. Time steps are on the x-axis, and the range from negative one to positive one is on the y-axis.)
/K 0
/P 7 0 R
/Pg 43 0 R
/S /Figure
/T (Figure)
>>
endobj
22 0 obj
<<
/A 49 0 R
/Alt (A line graph showing multiple signal channels over time steps. The channels, labeled Signal Ch 0 to Signal Ch 4, have fluctuating patterns until about the 230th time step, after which they stabilize. A red line represents the Grad-CAM overlay, which significantly increases around the 230th time step, stabilizing at about 2.0.)
/K 1
/P 7 0 R
/Pg 43 0 R
/S /Figure
/T (Figure)
>>
endobj
23 0 obj
<<
/A 49 0 R
/Alt (Line graph showing training and validation loss over 100 epochs. The blue line represents train loss, decreasing sharply at first and then leveling off around 0.02. The orange line shows validation loss, similarly dropping quickly before stabilizing slightly below train loss.)
/K 0
/P 7 0 R
/Pg 44 0 R
/S /Figure
/T (Figure)
>>
endobj
24 0 obj
<<
/A 49 0 R
/Alt (Line graph comparing true and predicted values using blue and orange lines. The x-axis ranges from 0 to 1500, and the y-axis ranges from 0 to 1.2. Both lines show high variability and overlap significantly.)
/K 1
/P 7 0 R
/Pg 44 0 R
/S /Figure
/T (Figure)
>>
endobj
25 0 obj
<<
/A 49 0 R
/Alt (Two graphs are displayed. The top graph shows fatigue index and motion quality over time with orange and green lines, respectively, on a score scale from 0 to 1 across 0 to 1500 sample indices. The bottom graph depicts emotional states by rule and cluster, with colored dots representing neutral, passive, relaxed, stressed, happy/excited, and fatigued states on a cluster scale from 0 to 3, also over 0 to 1500 sample indices.)
/K 0
/P 7 0 R
/Pg 45 0 R
/S /Figure
/T (Figure)
>>
endobj
